    "title": "Bekemeier leads Lady Bears past SFA in NCAA opener - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 hours ago\nAUSTIN, Tex–The Missouri State Lady Bears stepped onto the Big Dance floor.\nIt’s the NCAA tournament.\nAnd its a place the Lady Bears have been 18 times in their history.\nThis year’s edition starts in a First Four game against Stephen F. Austin.\nMissouri State was looking for its third win all-time against the LadyJacks.\nThe winner gets top-seeded Texas on Friday.\nAnd the Lady Bears going inside to Lainie Douglas and it’s a 10-4 MoState start.\nThen the Lady Bears go on an 11-nothing run, sparked by that Kaemyn Bekemeier three.\nFaith Lee then with the long two, the Lady Bears were up 21-8.\nStephen F. Austin answers from outside, Mica Perry with the corner three, it’s 24-21 after the first quarter.\nIn the second Maiesha Washington gets the loose ball and the scoop shot, Lady Bears up 34-33.\nEnd of the first half, Angel Scott, a former LadyJack, before transferring to MoState hits a three, Lady Bears up 47-43 at the half.\nAnd in the third quarter, another three by Bekemeier, and the Lady Bears lead 58-47 in the third quarter.\nBekemier had a double, double, 22 points and 13 rebounds and the Lady Bears win 85-75 to advance to face the Longhorns.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KOLR - OzarksFirst.com.",
